Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
tom holland is known for his commitment  to big action stunts and taking a hit or  two on set but how did he fare on those  super dangerous ones well we're here to  help figure those out here's to a look  behind some of tom's most dangerous  stunts and action sequences he decided  to take part in let's dive on in with a  harness of course  number one tom makes those spidey jumps  look so easy and even the ones where he  has to be so precise can get a little  nerve wracking as peter steals the  machina de cadavers from doctor strange  in no way home he jumps onto a moving  car and then backflips onto the ground  many would have thought this was all cgi  but no holland takes fate into his own  hands actually doing the stunt with a  moving car he wasn't all that free  having harnesses and whatnot but even  then he could have missed his mark and  serious injuries could have occurred we  know he's turned stunned professional  after his first two spider-man films but  this is just masterful number two all  those acrobatics are bound to get you  injured and with all the stress on your  knees they'll be the first to go that  was the fate of our poor peter parker  during a scene in no way home and this  one was pretty serious production forced  him to take a few days off to recuperate  which was nice but he was not all that  happy to be out he was really just  trying to find his way back saying i'm  chomping at the bid to get back to work  and back on set but the film's going  really well we're sure they had to  accommodate him with some knee braces  afterwards  number three dangerous stunts are not  something to laugh about but when the  persons involved come out of it with a  good laugh we can't help but laugh with  them as peter gets discovered by the  world as spider-man he freaks out a lot  prompting him to run around mae's  apartment in complete disarray and  apparently crash into stuff as well poor  holland got a little too excited on the  slippery floor and crashed right into an  unsecured bookshelf not only could this  have resulted in a bad head injury but  it could have derailed the whole film  though he was such a good sport about it  and got right back to filming the scene  number four tom was busy in 2021 filming  two back-to-back action blockbusters and  unfortunately with great action comes  great injury as uncharted got into the  thick of filming with the more dangerous  scenes holland faced his ultimate  challenge yet nathan drake jumps out of  a plane in midair dodging falling cars  and cargo boxes now to sell this kind of  a stunt tom was given pretty complex  instructions to keep him safe and sell  the stun but he wanted me to get hit and  then slide off that way so it took a  long time to get right number five  holland really went all out with the  stunts on this film there was never a  dull moment for him during filming as  this was about a treasure hunter  embarking on a dangerous adventure take  home injuries with a new norm but some  were a little too serious to just brush  off i walked away from every stunt but i  definitely limped from a few tom recalls  the scene where he took a pretty nasty  fall onto some roof tiles leaving him  with a badly bruised hip but he saw  these dangerous stunts as a way to make  the film even better  number six when you give a couple actors  some swords things can get a little cut  throat good thing that wasn't what it  resulted in for holland in this  uncharted sword fight but he didn't walk  away from it with a good outlook he  recalls his fight alongside co-star mark  wahlberg as one that he'd be glad never  to visit again we can't help but think  what if someone made a false move prop  swords can still hurt a lot but we're  glad that all he walked away with was a  bad outlook on sword fighting  number seven filling in the shoes as an  executive producer can give an actor a  lot more choices to work from uncharted  became very important to tom and he  wanted everything done with the most  effort felt that sense of responsibility  to bring this character to life he  trained for weeks to nail down those  dangerous stunts that we all know and  love from the video game when all is  said and done tom walked away with some  pretty nasty injuries from shooting but  to him that was all worth it i can  honestly say i have really done the work  to make this character you know live up  to your expectations in every way  possible  number eight holland's involvement in  chaos walking hit him a lot in the face  when he announced that he broke his nose  for the first time fans were to say the  least worried about his well-being it's  not the first time either that he'd  broken his nose but for this one it  probably could have been avoided as  director doug lyman prompted tom to do a  little flip in between takes he just  fell flat on his face holland puts it in  more layman's terms so i stood up i had  these stupid leather boots on i tried to  do a back flip and just broke my face  and right to the hospital he went maybe  put down a few cushions next time tom  number nine this behind the scenes  moment had us on the edge of our seats  for chaos walking we find our spidey  actors scaling walls yet again and we  sincerely all production designers use  prop paint it's not a big deal to see  tom climbing walls but when they're  rusty and he's jumping and grabbing  parts of the wall we get a little  concerned hopefully he had his tetanus  shots in order  number 10 with harnesses being a part of  tom's film career you'd think you'd feel  a little safe in them but taking a full  midair swing and holding your co-star in  the process can make things really risky  even zendaya had a nerve-wracking time  staying cool with spidey but little did  she know his peter tingle was on the  fritz with this stun  number 11 it's gonna take a little more  than a light rain shower to take this  spider out you'll need a whole lot of  cold water to get the job done  spider-man far from home fully initiated  holland into the stunt profession  enduring dozens of extreme stunts on big  locations but one in particular he was  not a fan of and this was the one where  peter gets slammed into a railing by a  blast of cold water as if the cold water  wasn't the worst of it he was hurled  into this railing multiple times to get  it right talk about back pain  number 12 getting stuck in a  free-falling elevator is not so fun but  what about lifting one yes we know tom  didn't actually lift an elevator but he  did have to hold his body up and crash  through the doors he was just getting  into stunt work and this one was  dangerous for the fact that there were  so many factors involved even though  there were some strings attached tom  just gave it his all facing the risk of  injury  number 13 all it took for parker to  become spider-man was a spider bite easy  enough and now he can do all the flips  and swings he wants holland on the other  hand had to train a lot to prepare for  the stunt heavy far from home he worked  closely with coordinators to train for  weeks leading up to filming but it  seemed nothing could prepare him for the  dangerous sequences he was about to do  number 14 since a lot of what spider-man  can do is superhuman it totally couldn't  have been done without the help of cgi  that didn't mean that tom got a little  break from the set but instead  he was fitted up with some motion  capture attire and put to work with some  stunts these acrobatics could have been  dangerous to do on an actual set so  doing it with all the necessary padding  sure was a load off for him  number 15 there's definitely a thrill in  performing dangerous stunts and holland  really worked with everyone to get the  best ones done collaborating with stunt  doubles and coordinators he was actually  allowed to perform some on the fly  stunts he imagined it really served his  character more this way making him a  pretty believable peter parker  number 16 if there's one thing tom  dislikes about stunt heavy films it's  harnesses there's no amount of prep you  can do to make a harness comfortable but  really we never really see him without  one while he's donning the suit or  nathan drake persona with his break from  acting we're sure we won't see tom near  one anytime soon we'd like to say no one  was hurt during the process but  unfortunately for tom he took home a few  injury trophies throughout the years  would you have fared as well as tom in  those scenes  let us know in the comments  [Music]

